}

`step` is the sequence step number when the finding sits inside a `TestCase_<n>`, otherwise null.
`where` is the class and method the defect is IN (`TestCase_14.main`, `TestSet.configure`); the
fix is routed by `where` alone, so name the unit that must change, not one the evidence mentions.
`kind` is exactly one of:
- `verdict_mismatch` — the verdict claims more, less or other than what the code checks
- `weak_observation` — passes on presence or CLI agreement instead of the observed value
- `wrong_symbol` — an unbound, fabricated or mis-used name, attribute, layer or signature
- `cross_unit_inconsistency` — units disagree on a shared convention (handles, ports, parsing)
- `missing_precondition` — state the step depends on is established by nothing
- `structural` — needs a new case, a moved step, or a verdict in the config-only setup (a design decision)
- `other` — none of the above; never invent a new tag
Order findings most severe first.
